</code></pre> <p>They are the first five events above, each printed as the whole record, with its <code>stream_type</code>. The run's log stays on stderr, so a pipe such as <code>| jq .key</code> reads only the records. YAML Blueprints lists the other ways to run a blueprint.</p> <p>While you edit the file, <code>desflow run first_shop.yaml --sample 5 --watch</code> runs it again each time the file changes. <code>--watch</code> needs the <code>watch</code> extra: <code>pip install "desflow[watch]"</code>, or <code>uv tool install "desflow[watch]"</code> for the command.</p> <p><code>desflow check first_shop.yaml</code> loads the file and reports its mistakes without running it, which is cheaper than finding them after a long run. It prints <code>ok</code> and the <code>sim_id</code> for a valid file.</p> <p><code>desflow</code> on its own lists every command, grouped by what it does, with examples. <code>desflow run --help</code> lists the options of <code>run</code>, also with examples. Command Line uses every command on one shop.</p>

